        "valueString": "Approximately 30–32; described as overweight."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-13",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-13",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Gait and mobility"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "effectiveDateTime": "2025-11-22",
        "valueString": "Slight antalgic gait, short stride and slow pace, cautious turning, and mild varus knees. Mobile and cautious. No walking aid; uses a banister on stairs."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-14",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-14",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Knee examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "effectiveDateTime": "2025-11-22",
        "valueString": "Mild bilateral bony enlargement and slight varus; small effusions, right greater than left. Mild bilateral medial joint-line tenderness. No erythema or warmth. No obvious ligament laxity on valgus/varus stress at 0° and 30°. Flexion to approximately 110° with end-range pain; extension near full; marked crepitus through range. McMurray negative for click or locking, with some medial discomfort only. No posterior tenderness or calf swelling."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-15",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-15",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Hand examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "effectiveDateTime": "2025-11-22",
        "valueString": "Several Heberden nodes at DIP joints and some PIP nodes, with mild tenderness. No synovial thickening or warmth. Range of motion preserved, with slight discomfort at end range."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-16",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-16",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Lower-limb neurological examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "effectiveDateTime": "2025-11-22",
        "valueString": "Power 5/5 in major muscle groups; light-touch sensation intact; reflexes normal; no focal deficit."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-17",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-17",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Targeted review for associated and red-flag symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "effectiveDateTime": "2025-11-22",
        "valueString": "Denies dizziness, syncope, chest pain, palpitations, new neurological symptoms, recent trauma, infection, or systemic symptoms. Denies fever, weight loss, night sweats, rash, eye inflammation, inflammatory back pain, bowel or bladder incontinence, saddle anaesthesia, peripheral paraesthesia, and focal weakness apart from subjective wobbly knees."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-18",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-18",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Patient attribution of joint symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "effectiveDateTime": "2025-11-22",
        "valueString": "Patient attributes symptoms to a cheap mattress, chemicals in food, and deterioration since COVID vaccinations."
      }
    },
